.TH SYSML 1 "" "sysml 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sysml \- command line tool for the SysML Editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sysml
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B sysml
.BR \-h " | " \-\-help
.br
.B sysml
.BR \-V " | " \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sysml
installs the Claude agent skills that ship with the SysML Editor VS Code extension.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B skills
Install the skills sysml-modeling, sysml-tutor and sysml-ui-testing.
.TP
.BI help " command"
Show help for a command.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SS sysml skills [options]
Copies the skills into a Claude skills folder. A skill that is already installed and identical is skipped. A skill that differs is refused unless
.B \-f
is given.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-project
Install into ./.claude/skills instead of ~/.claude/skills.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dir =\fIDIR\fR
Install into DIR (each skill becomes DIR/<name>).
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Overwrite skills that differ from the bundled ones.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Show what would be done without changing anything.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Print nothing, not even with \-v.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print one line per skill.
.TP
.B \-\-
End of options.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sysml skills                       Install for your user
sysml skills \-p                    Install into the current project
sysml skills \-pf                   Project install, overwriting changed skills
sysml skills \-n \-v                 Show what would happen
sysml skills \-d ~/work/skills      Install into a custom folder
sysml skills \-\-dir=./skills \-v     Same, with the long option
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on failure, 2 on a usage error. Errors are printed to standard error as "sysml: <message>", followed by the help page of the command. Nothing is printed on success unless \-v is given. Colour is used only on a terminal and never when NO_COLOR is set.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.claude/skills
Default install folder.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/GarrettGruss/sysml-editor
